WEBVTT

00:00:00.781 --> 00:00:06.242
Hi. Welcome to Steadfast
Men. This is Lesson One.

00:00:06.482 --> 00:00:10.003
Today's lesson is called A Quiet Tuesday.

00:00:10.263 --> 00:00:12.504
Here's what you and I are going to cover.

00:00:12.824 --> 00:00:18.805
First, what I mean by a Tuesday, and
why God builds a man on the plain

00:00:18.845 --> 00:00:19.685
days.

00:00:20.126 --> 00:00:24.927
Second, why being busy isn't
the same as being there.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:29.108
Third, the first mark of a steadfast man.

00:00:29.248 --> 00:00:35.289
It's called Stop Waiting. Then the
reasons you might give me for waiting,

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:37.329
and one move for you to make

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:41.591
I'm Wes. Wes Hart. I'm a husband.

00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:46.172
I'm a dad. I've got a job I
go to every day, same as you.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:50.313
And for the next twenty-four lessons,
I'm going to be your teacher.

00:00:51.393 --> 00:00:53.253
I don't know where you are right now.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:57.414
Maybe the kids are finally asleep
and you've got the laptop open.

00:00:57.675 --> 00:01:01.735
Maybe you're in your truck on a lunch
break with your phone propped on the wheel.

00:01:01.996 --> 00:01:05.576
Maybe a buddy sent you the link
and you're giving it five minutes.

00:01:05.836 --> 00:01:09.197
Wherever you are, I'm
glad you clicked on this.

00:01:09.357 --> 00:01:12.118
I mean that. And I'd bet on something.

00:01:12.178 --> 00:01:17.339
You told somebody, or maybe just yourself,
that you were only going to check this

00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:20.460
out. Just looking. No promises.

00:01:21.387 --> 00:01:24.548
That's fine. I started out that way too.

00:01:24.948 --> 00:01:26.048
I'm still here.

00:01:26.428 --> 00:01:30.549
So before you get going, I want
you to hear one thing from me.

00:01:31.109 --> 00:01:32.790
You're on time.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:38.431
Maybe you're young, and you're still waiting
for somebody to tell you you're a man.

00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:40.472
You're on time.

00:01:40.892 --> 00:01:44.993
Maybe you're married and your kids
are climbing all over you every night.

00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:46.913
You're on time.

00:01:47.313 --> 00:01:52.515
Maybe you're divorced, you're still
a dad, and the house got real quiet.

00:01:52.815 --> 00:01:54.495
You're on time.

00:01:54.915 --> 00:01:57.676
Maybe you figured this
was for somebody younger.

00:01:58.096 --> 00:02:01.517
You're on time. You're not a guest here.

00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:03.037
This is yours.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.978
So here's what I'll promise you.

00:02:06.338 --> 00:02:09.979
I won't waste your time. I'm
not going to yell at you.

00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:13.200
And I'm not going to tell you
everything's fine, either.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.880
I'm going to teach you something true.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.161
I'll show you where it
shows up in a normal day.

00:02:19.421 --> 00:02:22.282
Then I'll give you one thing to go do.

00:02:23.122 --> 00:02:25.483
Okay. Here's how this goes.

00:02:25.803 --> 00:02:28.843
You and I do this one lesson at a time.

00:02:28.904 --> 00:02:30.344
Twenty-four of them.

00:02:30.765 --> 00:02:31.465
One.

00:02:31.945 --> 00:02:37.867
Then the next one. Every lesson is built
the same way, so you'll always know where

00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:42.328
you are. First, I teach. That's this part.

00:02:43.115 --> 00:02:46.456
Have your Bible open and
your workbook next to you.

00:02:46.636 --> 00:02:50.777
If you don't have the workbook
yet, a notebook and a pen are fine.

00:02:51.157 --> 00:02:54.077
Second, you stop and think.

00:02:54.397 --> 00:02:59.598
A few times in every lesson I'll ask you
to pause this and write something down.

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:03.999
Don't skip those. That's where
the lesson becomes yours.

00:03:04.279 --> 00:03:08.120
And third, you walk away with one move.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.362
One. Not a list. One thing you
actually go do on a normal day, with

00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:16.082
the people in your life.

00:03:16.442 --> 00:03:20.683
Why just one? Because I've
been handed plenty of lists.

00:03:20.803 --> 00:03:24.684
You have too. A list
feels great on Sunday.

00:03:24.784 --> 00:03:28.885
By Wednesday it's on the floor of
the truck with the fast-food bags.

00:03:29.285 --> 00:03:31.625
One move you can actually do.

00:03:32.005 --> 00:03:36.766
And at the start of the next lesson, the
first thing I'll ask you is how it went.

00:03:36.946 --> 00:03:40.707
If you've got a friend doing this
with you, he's going to ask you too.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.568
Let him. That's the whole plan.

00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:47.329
Show up. Tell the truth. Do the move.

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:50.949
So get a pen. Turn your phone face down.

00:03:51.049 --> 00:03:52.410
Let's get to work.

00:03:53.997 --> 00:03:56.457
Here's the big idea of this lesson.

00:03:56.597 --> 00:04:00.498
If you only remember one
sentence, make it this one.

00:04:00.758 --> 00:04:05.338
A man's life gets decided on
the days nobody photographs.

00:04:06.778 --> 00:04:08.159
Say that to yourself.

00:04:08.499 --> 00:04:11.359
The days nobody photographs.

00:04:11.799 --> 00:04:14.679
Think about the days
that do get photographed.

00:04:14.839 --> 00:04:18.120
Your wedding. A baby. A new job.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.280
Those days are real. God uses them.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.601
I've got nothing against a big day.

00:04:23.821 --> 00:04:28.361
But let me ask you something. Have you
ever had one of those days you were sure

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:31.281
would change you? A vow you meant.

00:04:31.362 --> 00:04:36.922
A night in a hospital hallway. A Sunday
you walked out of church a different man.

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:42.563
Be honest with me. Did the next ordinary
day look a lot like the ordinary day before

00:04:42.603 --> 00:04:43.123
it?

00:04:44.223 --> 00:04:45.863
Yeah. Mine too.

00:04:46.283 --> 00:04:50.224
A big day can mark you.
It can't give you a habit.

00:04:50.444 --> 00:04:53.744
A habit is what a lot of
plain days leave on you.

00:04:53.924 --> 00:04:55.924
And most of your days aren't big.

00:04:56.024 --> 00:04:58.304
Most of them are just Tuesday.

00:04:58.684 --> 00:05:03.105
Jesus put it this way. Luke
chapter sixteen, verse ten.

00:05:03.952 --> 00:05:09.834
"Whoever can be trusted with very little
can also be trusted with much, and whoever

00:05:09.874 --> 00:05:14.375
is dishonest with very little
will also be dishonest with much."

00:05:15.576 --> 00:05:18.056
Let's slow down and actually read that.

00:05:18.116 --> 00:05:19.317
Look at it with me.

00:05:19.677 --> 00:05:22.197
Jesus is talking about a manager.

00:05:22.298 --> 00:05:25.098
A man who's in charge of
somebody else's money.

00:05:25.378 --> 00:05:28.659
And look at what He measures.
Not the big account.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.181
The small one. Two words
show up twice in that verse.

00:05:33.261 --> 00:05:34.321
Did you catch them?

00:05:34.661 --> 00:05:37.882
Very little. That's Tuesday talk.

00:05:38.162 --> 00:05:41.243
Very little is the tone
you use when you're tired.

00:05:41.303 --> 00:05:45.284
It's a text you owe somebody.
It's ten minutes with your kid.

00:05:45.505 --> 00:05:50.826
And the verse cuts both ways.
Trusted in little, trusted in much.

00:05:51.046 --> 00:05:54.367
Dishonest in little, dishonest in much.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:57.188
The small stuff doesn't stay small.

00:05:57.288 --> 00:05:59.949
It shows up again when
the stakes get bigger.

00:06:00.189 --> 00:06:03.630
So let me ask you. Where
does God build a man?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.351
On the big day? Or on the plain one?

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:09.332
The plain one. The very little.

00:06:09.492 --> 00:06:12.173
That's this whole lesson in two words.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:19.521
Okay. Here's the first point. What
do I mean when I say a Tuesday?

00:06:20.001 --> 00:06:23.661
I mean a day with nothing
on it worth dressing up for.

00:06:23.921 --> 00:06:28.062
You come home tired. Or you
never left the apartment.

00:06:28.142 --> 00:06:31.322
And the loudest thing in
the house is your phone.

00:06:31.502 --> 00:06:34.763
And right in front of
you there's a small yes.

00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:37.843
Something you could say. Or swallow.

00:06:38.323 --> 00:06:43.824
I call it a Tuesday. If your hard
day is Thursday, call it Thursday.

00:06:43.964 --> 00:06:47.244
The name doesn't matter. The day does.

00:06:47.624 --> 00:06:50.285
I'll tell you how I dodge my Tuesdays.

00:06:50.405 --> 00:06:56.486
I'm really good at it. I've prayed
out loud, "God, make me a better man."

00:06:56.746 --> 00:07:01.246
Then I spent the next half hour on
my phone comparing leaf blowers.

00:07:01.526 --> 00:07:05.507
Thirty minutes. Reviews. Decibel ratings.

00:07:05.647 --> 00:07:09.227
The prayer was real. The
phone was just easier.

00:07:09.707 --> 00:07:11.808
I'd guess you're a little like that too.

00:07:11.948 --> 00:07:14.428
You'll research a tool for an hour.

00:07:14.508 --> 00:07:17.408
You won't look at your
own day for five minutes.

00:07:18.208 --> 00:07:23.109
Let me tell you about one of my Tuesdays,
so you know I'm not talking down to you.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:28.430
My daughter had a bike. The back tire
had been soft for a couple of days.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:29.570
Maybe four.

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:34.691
One afternoon she met me at the
door and said, "Dad, can we fix it?

00:07:34.751 --> 00:07:35.611
Together?"

00:07:35.991 --> 00:07:38.891
It wasn't a crisis. It was a tire.

00:07:39.191 --> 00:07:42.532
I said, "After supper." And I meant it.

00:07:42.712 --> 00:07:46.632
Right then, I was a good dad. We ate.

00:07:46.792 --> 00:07:51.973
Then I opened my laptop, because there was
one thing I didn't want hanging over me

00:07:52.013 --> 00:07:53.033
in the morning.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.080
One thing.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.300
That's what I told myself.

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:00.081
It turned into the next thing.

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:02.801
I could hear her in the other room.

00:08:03.161 --> 00:08:07.801
At some point she rolled the bike out to
the edge of the patio and went back to her

00:08:07.841 --> 00:08:08.741
homework.

00:08:09.142 --> 00:08:10.662
I didn't see her do it.

00:08:11.242 --> 00:08:13.782
Late that night I let the dog out.

00:08:13.822 --> 00:08:16.822
Porch light on. And there's the bike.

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:18.802
Tire still soft.

00:08:19.182 --> 00:08:23.583
The pump was in the hall closet, right
where I'd pictured the two of us getting it

00:08:23.623 --> 00:08:24.263
out.

00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:28.983
So I fixed it. In the dark. By myself.

00:08:29.363 --> 00:08:31.104
And I felt useful.

00:08:31.424 --> 00:08:35.664
That's a dangerous feeling for
a man who just missed the point.

00:08:36.244 --> 00:08:40.045
The next morning she saw
the tire and said, "Oh.

00:08:40.225 --> 00:08:41.065
Thanks."

00:08:41.545 --> 00:08:43.065
That was all she said.

00:08:43.365 --> 00:08:45.625
She'd already stopped waiting on me.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.705
I did the job. And I missed my girl.

00:08:50.886 --> 00:08:53.066
Let's stop right here for a minute.

00:08:53.246 --> 00:08:56.706
Think about yesterday. Just yesterday.

00:08:56.926 --> 00:09:01.047
Find one small yes that
was right in front of you.

00:09:01.187 --> 00:09:04.987
A person. Not a task. Did you say it?

00:09:05.147 --> 00:09:06.687
Or did you swallow it?

00:09:07.787 --> 00:09:10.287
Open your workbook to Lesson One.

00:09:10.428 --> 00:09:15.048
In the margin, write one word
for where you went instead.

00:09:15.308 --> 00:09:20.869
Phone. Work. Later.
Tired. Whatever's true.

00:09:21.049 --> 00:09:25.229
Nobody else has to see it.
Just be honest with the page.

00:09:25.409 --> 00:09:27.389
Pause this and write it.

00:09:29.469 --> 00:09:32.710
Got it? Good. Hang on to that word.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.270
I'm coming back to it.

00:09:35.897 --> 00:09:39.138
Here's the second point,
and this one's sneaky.

00:09:39.658 --> 00:09:42.738
That night with the bike, I wasn't lazy.

00:09:43.079 --> 00:09:44.219
I was busy.

00:09:44.719 --> 00:09:47.179
And busy will lie to you.

00:09:47.499 --> 00:09:49.260
The lie goes like this.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.800
"I was busy, so I must have been there."

00:09:53.261 --> 00:09:54.661
I wasn't there.

00:09:55.081 --> 00:09:58.722
Busy is an easy place
for a good man to hide.

00:09:58.862 --> 00:10:01.882
He's competent, so nobody looks closer.

00:10:02.183 --> 00:10:06.023
If you're getting things
done, nobody asks questions.

00:10:06.243 --> 00:10:07.584
Least of all you.

00:10:08.164 --> 00:10:11.264
Here's another one. This
one's about my wife.

00:10:11.705 --> 00:10:14.285
A while back I owed her an apology.

00:10:14.725 --> 00:10:15.925
One sentence.

00:10:16.246 --> 00:10:20.467
I'd been short with her and then I
acted like it had worn off on its own.

00:10:20.827 --> 00:10:23.787
I practiced it at a red
light on the way home.

00:10:24.027 --> 00:10:28.568
I had the true sentence ready. The
one that would cost me something.

00:10:28.888 --> 00:10:33.009
And I had a softer one behind
it, in case I lost my nerve.

00:10:33.309 --> 00:10:37.550
By the time I pulled into the
driveway, the true one was gone.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:40.791
I walked in and said, "Long day."

00:10:41.291 --> 00:10:45.152
She got a weather report. I
got to feel like I'd shown up.

00:10:45.372 --> 00:10:51.013
We were three feet apart, and I was finishing
a conversation she was never part of.

00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:57.454
Years ago an older man I trusted asked
me a question I still don't enjoy.

00:10:57.775 --> 00:10:59.855
He'd earned the right to ask it.

00:11:00.602 --> 00:11:04.943
He said, "What did you do yesterday that
the people in your house couldn't have

00:11:04.983 --> 00:11:06.063
hired out?"

00:11:06.463 --> 00:11:09.704
I had my answer ready.
I'd worked a full day.

00:11:09.844 --> 00:11:13.985
I'd fixed a dripping faucet. I'd
cleared out a pile of messages.

00:11:14.225 --> 00:11:17.586
I handed him that list the
way a boy turns in homework.

00:11:17.946 --> 00:11:21.527
He nodded. Patient. Almost kind.

00:11:21.807 --> 00:11:25.308
And then he said, "I didn't
ask what you finished.

00:11:25.508 --> 00:11:27.448
I asked where you were."

00:11:28.669 --> 00:11:30.949
That question still stops me.

00:11:31.289 --> 00:11:36.031
You can be the hero of your to-do
list and a stranger in your own house.

00:11:36.151 --> 00:11:39.311
And if you live alone,
nobody's there to push back.

00:11:39.411 --> 00:11:41.492
It's easy to let yourself off.

00:11:42.052 --> 00:11:44.473
So is this about doing less?

00:11:44.873 --> 00:11:49.314
No. The tire needed air.
The faucet needed fixing.

00:11:49.434 --> 00:11:53.815
Work is good. It's about
where you are while you do it.

00:11:53.875 --> 00:11:56.175
Not how much. Where.

00:11:57.376 --> 00:11:59.756
Let's put together what we've got so far.

00:12:00.177 --> 00:12:05.278
One. A man's life gets decided
on the days nobody photographs.

00:12:05.538 --> 00:12:06.218
Two.

00:12:06.618 --> 00:12:09.139
God builds you in the very little.

00:12:09.419 --> 00:12:10.159
Three.

00:12:10.559 --> 00:12:16.540
Busy is not the same as there. If any of
that's fuzzy, go back and catch it again.

00:12:16.661 --> 00:12:18.701
I'll wait. I'm good at waiting.

00:12:18.881 --> 00:12:21.542
And that's exactly the problem.

00:12:23.149 --> 00:12:26.690
Here's the third point.
And this one has a name.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:31.311
Over these lessons you'll learn
four marks of a steadfast man.

00:12:31.431 --> 00:12:33.591
Today you get the first one.

00:12:33.891 --> 00:12:37.492
Stop Waiting. Here's the
verse that goes with it.

00:12:37.572 --> 00:12:40.373
James chapter four, verse seventeen.

00:12:40.773 --> 00:12:46.594
"If anyone, then, knows the good they ought
to do and doesn't do it, it is sin for

00:12:46.634 --> 00:12:47.254
them."

00:12:48.475 --> 00:12:53.136
Read that one slowly. It doesn't
say, does something terrible.

00:12:53.176 --> 00:12:57.217
It says, knows the
good, and doesn't do it.

00:12:57.417 --> 00:13:00.377
That's waiting. You know the yes.

00:13:00.437 --> 00:13:04.618
You just put it off. You're
probably not refusing to show up.

00:13:04.718 --> 00:13:07.259
You're waiting. I know I do it.

00:13:07.459 --> 00:13:10.800
Waiting for a better season.
Waiting to feel ready.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:14.901
Waiting for after supper. Let
me tell you about my twenties.

00:13:15.221 --> 00:13:19.322
I figured manhood would show up one
day like a package on the porch.

00:13:19.562 --> 00:13:24.983
Some morning I'd wake up, the hesitation
would be gone, and real life would start.

00:13:25.223 --> 00:13:29.864
The package never came. The hesitation
just got older along with me.

00:13:30.684 --> 00:13:35.065
Paul wrote about this. First
Corinthians thirteen, verse eleven.

00:13:35.285 --> 00:13:40.747
"When I was a child, I talked like a child,
I thought like a child, I reasoned like

00:13:40.787 --> 00:13:46.048
a child. When I became a man, I put
the ways of childhood behind me."

00:13:47.255 --> 00:13:49.975
Look at the first half. Talked.

00:13:50.195 --> 00:13:56.436
Thought. Reasoned. He doesn't say,
when I was a child I had toys.

00:13:56.777 --> 00:13:59.257
All three of those are on the inside.

00:13:59.397 --> 00:14:04.958
You can have a mortgage, a title, and a
good name, and still be thinking like a boy.

00:14:05.298 --> 00:14:06.978
Now look at the second half.

00:14:07.338 --> 00:14:11.539
I put them behind me. They
didn't fall off on his birthday.

00:14:11.619 --> 00:14:14.439
He put them there. On purpose.

00:14:14.799 --> 00:14:18.800
A boy's yes is real. That's
what makes it tricky.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.541
It lasts exactly as long
as the feeling behind it.

00:14:22.721 --> 00:14:26.721
A man's yes is still standing
after the feeling's gone.

00:14:26.921 --> 00:14:30.882
Now, stop waiting doesn't
mean stop resting.

00:14:30.942 --> 00:14:35.363
Hear me on that. Rest is
good. A nap is allowed.

00:14:35.443 --> 00:14:39.903
A quiet evening is a gift.
Waiting is something else.

00:14:40.063 --> 00:14:44.684
Waiting is being gone from what's yours
while you keep busy with something else.

00:14:45.904 --> 00:14:49.405
Pause again. What are you
waiting on before you start?

00:14:49.465 --> 00:14:52.885
A better job? A wife? A clearer head?

00:14:53.005 --> 00:14:56.706
Your dad to finally say it?
Write it under your word.

00:14:56.786 --> 00:14:58.746
Just the thing you're waiting on.

00:15:00.867 --> 00:15:06.268
Okay. Now look at it and ask yourself,
is that really mine to wait on?

00:15:06.368 --> 00:15:07.968
Or is it mine to start?

00:15:09.555 --> 00:15:11.876
You might already be arguing with me.

00:15:12.056 --> 00:15:15.376
That's good. Let's take
those one at a time.

00:15:15.457 --> 00:15:16.417
First one.

00:15:16.817 --> 00:15:19.177
"Wes, I'm just tired."

00:15:19.598 --> 00:15:23.178
I believe you. You might be
carrying a lot right now.

00:15:23.459 --> 00:15:25.959
A job that takes everything it can.

00:15:26.019 --> 00:15:27.880
A house full of need.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:33.301
If you're barely holding on, hear
this as an invitation, not a whip.

00:15:33.661 --> 00:15:37.202
Some nights, going to sleep
is the faithful thing.

00:15:37.442 --> 00:15:42.543
But if you're just comfortable being
gone, don't borrow the tired man's excuse.

00:15:42.724 --> 00:15:46.985
God knows which one you are.
And honestly, so do you.

00:15:47.785 --> 00:15:48.825
Second one.

00:15:49.205 --> 00:15:55.167
"Nobody ever showed me how." That's true
for more fathers and sons than you'd think.

00:15:55.407 --> 00:16:01.088
Nobody stood next to you on a plain day
and said, here, this is what a man does.

00:16:01.368 --> 00:16:04.749
I'm not blaming you for that.
But look at the verse again.

00:16:04.869 --> 00:16:09.190
Paul didn't say, when my
father finally did his job.

00:16:09.311 --> 00:16:14.672
He said, when I became a man, I put
the ways of childhood behind me.

00:16:14.932 --> 00:16:18.393
That door's open whether
anybody showed you or not.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:20.300
Third one.

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:25.382
"I'm too old. I'm retired.
That's for a younger man."

00:16:26.102 --> 00:16:29.743
I know a man I'll call
Howard. Late sixties.

00:16:29.863 --> 00:16:36.025
Retired, and he earned it. His grandson
asked him to come see a project at school.

00:16:36.365 --> 00:16:39.526
Howard said he was tired. He was.

00:16:39.786 --> 00:16:45.148
He went anyway. And on the ride
home, that boy talked the whole way.

00:16:45.548 --> 00:16:47.628
Howard called me that night and said,

00:16:47.929 --> 00:16:51.509
"I thought the job was over.
The boy didn't get the memo."

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:57.031
The job might be over. Being a
man didn't clock out with it.

00:16:57.831 --> 00:16:58.952
And one more.

00:16:59.272 --> 00:17:03.713
"I'm single. I live alone.
Who am I even showing up for?"

00:17:04.233 --> 00:17:07.254
Somebody you can reach still needs you.

00:17:07.434 --> 00:17:12.396
A brother. A friend. A kid at church
who doesn't have a dad around.

00:17:12.676 --> 00:17:16.977
And God, who's been in that
apartment with you the whole time.

00:17:17.217 --> 00:17:19.258
He's seen your Tuesday already.

00:17:19.538 --> 00:17:22.099
Show up for it where He can see it.

00:17:23.706 --> 00:17:26.987
So what does this look like
on a real Monday morning?

00:17:27.067 --> 00:17:29.787
Let's get practical. You wake up.

00:17:30.028 --> 00:17:33.608
Before you open your phone,
you ask one question.

00:17:33.808 --> 00:17:37.269
Who's mine today? Not what's on my list.

00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:38.769
Who's mine.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:43.951
At breakfast, if your kid starts telling
you something, you put the cup down and

00:17:43.991 --> 00:17:46.731
look at your kid. Thirty seconds.

00:17:47.071 --> 00:17:50.632
On the drive in, you send the
text you've been putting off.

00:17:50.772 --> 00:17:52.873
The one you know you owe.

00:17:53.193 --> 00:17:57.214
At work, you do the job
well. That's part of it too.

00:17:57.474 --> 00:18:02.435
And when you walk in the door that night,
the true sentence comes out before "long

00:18:02.475 --> 00:18:03.675
day" does.

00:18:04.015 --> 00:18:06.656
Nobody's going to photograph any of that.

00:18:06.816 --> 00:18:08.276
All of it counts.

00:18:09.477 --> 00:18:12.657
Okay. So here's your one move.

00:18:13.017 --> 00:18:16.879
One. eat one meal with
your phone in another room.

00:18:17.079 --> 00:18:20.719
Not in your pocket. Not face
down next to your plate.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:25.921
In another room. If you live
alone, you still sit down to eat.

00:18:26.021 --> 00:18:28.681
And the phone still
goes in the other room.

00:18:29.062 --> 00:18:33.222
Then one more piece.
Text one man you trust.

00:18:33.403 --> 00:18:36.103
Ask him, "What did you
do with your Tuesday?"

00:18:36.343 --> 00:18:37.923
And let him ask you back.

00:18:38.264 --> 00:18:41.004
Send it before you turn
this off, if you can.

00:18:41.244 --> 00:18:45.945
A Tuesday nobody else knows about
is a Tuesday you'll explain away.

00:18:46.766 --> 00:18:50.706
Last pause. Write the
move in your own words.

00:18:51.007 --> 00:18:55.348
My next move on a Tuesday
is. Put a day on it.

00:18:55.428 --> 00:18:59.789
Put a meal on it. Put down the
name of the man you'll text.

00:19:01.896 --> 00:19:05.037
Good. That's a move you can fail at.

00:19:05.197 --> 00:19:08.257
And that's the only kind
that can make a man.

00:19:09.058 --> 00:19:11.158
Let's go over it one more time.

00:19:11.418 --> 00:19:15.879
A man's life gets decided on
the days nobody photographs.

00:19:16.199 --> 00:19:18.860
God builds you in the very little.

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:25.061
Busy is not the same as there. And
the first mark of a steadfast man is

00:19:25.101 --> 00:19:30.242
Stop Waiting. The last ordinary
day is the one you answer for.

00:19:30.382 --> 00:19:33.343
The next one is the one you practice on.

00:19:34.763 --> 00:19:39.504
If you trust Christ, you're not trying
to earn your way into anything here.

00:19:39.625 --> 00:19:42.225
Your Father has already claimed you.

00:19:42.405 --> 00:19:46.266
You put the childish ways down
because you belong to Him.

00:19:46.346 --> 00:19:50.907
Not so He'll take you. And if you're not
sure about Him yet, you're still welcome

00:19:50.947 --> 00:19:54.108
here. Start with one honest day.

00:19:54.248 --> 00:19:56.928
He's never been afraid of an honest man.

00:19:57.729 --> 00:19:59.889
Look at the word you wrote in the margin.

00:20:00.089 --> 00:20:02.470
That's where your Tuesday goes missing.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.090
Go show up for it.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:08.291
Next lesson we look at
why that's been so hard.

00:20:08.371 --> 00:20:12.192
Why a good man keeps waiting,
even when he knows better.

00:20:12.372 --> 00:20:14.892
You said you were just
going to check this out.

00:20:15.053 --> 00:20:18.073
You stayed. That was your first yes.

00:20:18.213 --> 00:20:21.314
Don't waste it. I'll see
you in the next lesson.
